# verible-verilog-lint --rules_config file.
# One rule per line: +rule enables (with =param:value;... for parameters), -rule disables.
# Verible's default rule set stays on; these lines add, tune or disable on top of it.
# Severities (error vs warning) are NOT decided here but in rules.toml.
# Verible reports at most one finding per token location: when two rules fire on the same
# token (e.g. explicit-begin and always-comb on the same `always`), the second appears only
# after the first is fixed. Verilator and the custom checks cover the gap.

+line-length=length:100
+parameter-name-style=localparam_style:ALL_CAPS;parameter_style:ALL_CAPS
+explicit-parameter-storage-type
+explicit-begin
+signal-name-style
+one-module-per-file
+suspicious-semicolon
+mismatched-labels
+instance-shadowing
+legacy-generate-region
+forbid-negative-array-dim

# AXI / valid-ready ports carry protocol suffixes (_valid, _ready, _tdata), not _i/_o.
-port-name-suffix
